# Same public values as .env.production, so a fresh clone runs `npm run dev`
# with no setup. These keys are public by design: they ship inside the browser
# bundle on a public site, and Row Level Security is what protects the data.
# Real secrets (the Discord client secret, the service-role key, test-user
# passwords) never belong in a committed file.
